Civil 3D MCP engineering audit | v0.21.0 | 2026-11-25
====================================================

Executive summary
-----------------
The validated source is suitable for supervised local use on a verified
target drawing. Broader workspace deployment still needs file authorization,
bounded workloads and explicit recovery contracts for multi-stage imports.
Native profile edits can silently remove vertical curves or commit without a
requested curve. Treat that as a blocker for production use of those actions.

The audited runtime is the Python stdio server, its bundled entry point, the
private loopback bridge, and native code paths supporting the findings below.
The loopback protocol and its correlation IDs are private to this project.
MCP and JSON-RPC requirements apply at the public stdio boundary. The optional
external ChatGPT tunnel is client-side configuration in this repository.
ChatGPT and Claude applications and the tunnel were outside live verification.

Evidence types used below are source-confirmed, observed on the installed
dependency, and conditional on specific inputs or deployment. Line numbers
refer to the patched workspace. Findings marked Fixed include code changes in
this task. The workspace had no Git baseline. Earlier audit files remain as
historical records.

Critical
--------
No Critical finding was established under the local workstation trust model
and the interfaces inspected. The project should still address the High
findings before exposing additional client identities or enabling native profile
edits on production drawings.

High
----
H1 | Edit integrity | Fixed | plugin/Bridge/EditRequests.cs:56-100
The previous ledger evicted old request identities after reaching its entry
limit. An identical retry of a previously committed edit could execute again.
It also allowed retries of every state=error even when execution had begun.
The patch retains identity and outcome for the session, refuses new IDs at
8,192 entries, and allows the same ID to run again only for the typed queue
timeout that proves the native delegate never began. Full receipt caching
remains bounded. At saturation, restart Civil 3D and read the drawing to get
new identifiers. A durable per-drawing stage history would remove the restart
requirement and allow cross-session recovery.

H2 | Cancellation and calling order | Fixed for later stages |
server/server.py:140-181 and server/bridge_client.py:72-129
A cancelled stdio request could leave the synchronous worker executing later
write stages. The patch propagates a cancellation signal to that worker and
checks it before subsequent bridge requests and at send time. Once Civil 3D
accepts a request, it may finish and must be reconciled through edit status.
An absolute deadline and safely interruptible read/parse jobs remain open.
Specification reference at the end of this report.

H3 | MCP tool error propagation | Fixed | server/server.py:56-71
Native receipts for denied edits, rolled-back edits and failed after-commit
work could be sent as successful tool calls. Failed or partial workflows could
have the same issue. The patch sets isError and preserves the receipt in JSON
text and structuredContent. Pending operations and successful dry runs remain
normal responses. JSON-RPC request errors stay at the protocol layer.

H4 | Local file authorization | Open, deployment-dependent |
plugin/Read/SheetRead.cs:196-198, plugin/Edit/BlockOps.cs:126-142,
server/sewergems.py:69-111, server/watergems.py:115-123 and README.md:113-139
Read-only mode permits inspect_file and workbook/CSV checking actions. They
take client-selected paths and read with the host Windows user's existing
permissions. There is no project-root policy at those entry points. This also
applies when an external tunnel starts the server with --read-only. The data
visible depends on the Windows account, server configuration and connected
workspace participants. Canonicalize local paths against administrator-approved
roots, verify symlink/reparse-point behavior, handle UNC paths explicitly and
apply a common policy for every read and write path. Native file inspection
also needs a process-level boundary where robust isolation is required.

H5 | Geometry loss | Open, source-confirmed |
plugin/Edit/AlignmentOps.cs:117-156 and :187-221
An elevation-only change removes the existing PVI and replaces it with a
tangent PVI when curve data was omitted. Curve creation also catches any
exception, can restore a tangent PVI and returns a warning, so the outer
transaction can commit without the requested geometry. Distinguish omitted
curve data from explicit curve removal, preserve the existing curve on an
elevation-only move, and let explicit curve creation errors roll back the edit.
Verify parabola, asymmetric and circular cases on the native releases before
shipping the geometry change.

H6 | Partial workflows and recovery | Partially fixed |
server/watergems.py:728-822 and server/sewergems.py:680-735
The network transaction commits before dependent profile/layout/report work.
WaterGEMS does further work after that commit outside the broad stage handler,
including preparation before the try block and postflight cover reporting.
An exception there can omit the committed-network receipt. When the cached
core reply expires, WaterGEMS explicitly lacks the part handles it needs to
resume. The patch fixes SewerGEMS finish-stage recovery after a known pre-start
timeout by retrying the same ID. The ledger verifies that the regenerated
operation parameters still match. Persist stage state and
needed object references, validate and plan independent stages before commit,
make postflight errors return the committed-stage receipt. Exercise interruption
at every commit boundary.

H7 | Native work budget | Open, input-dependent |
plugin/Read/GeometryRead.cs:200-201, :302-313 and
plugin/Read/CivilRead.cs:214-262
Fallback material sampling divides segment length by a caller-supplied positive
step, narrows the result to int and loops with no aggregate budget. Very small
steps can create excessive work or exceed the int conversion range. Pipe
interference scans pairs and retains all matching results before taking the
output limit. The operations run on the Civil 3D application thread. Validate
the segment ratio before the cast, cap aggregate samples, add a spatial
candidate index and retain the bounded best hits while tracking total matches.

H8 | Upgrade can remove a read-only client setting | Open, source-confirmed |
package/configure_clients.ps1:51-65 and :82-104
When changing an existing Claude command path, the installer replaces the
whole civil3d object with a command-only object. The Codex updater replaces
the entire table and sub-tables, even at the same executable path when extra
settings exist. An existing args=["--read-only"] or split-mode environment can
be lost and the tool exposure can change. The native drawing permission still
applies. Change only the command key, preserve args/env and other user fields,
validate staged JSON or TOML before atomic replacement, and test upgrades with
existing read-only configurations. No client settings were changed in this
audit.

Medium
------
M1 | SDK lifecycle | Open, observed on MCP Python SDK 1.30.0 |
server/server.py:190-232 and installed mcp/server/session.py:175-214
The SDK accepted tools/list after initialize without notifications/initialized.
More importantly, notifications/initialized followed by tools/list worked
without any initialize request. The former violates the client-side sequence,
and by itself does not demonstrate failure with a compliant client. The latter
shows that the SDK can enter its ready state without version/capability
negotiation. Require ordered session state in an upstream SDK fix or a tested
transport adapter. Keep valid initialize, ping and notification tests alongside
the out-of-order cases.

M2 | JSON-RPC error mapping | Open, observed on MCP Python SDK 1.30.0 |
installed mcp/shared/session.py:366-394, mcp/server/stdio.py:66-79
and mcp/server/lowlevel/server.py:708-719
After successful initialization an unrecognized method returned -32602
(Invalid params) instead of -32601 (Method not found). A malformed JSON line
produced notifications/message without a -32700 parse-error response with a
null ID. Fix dispatch and parsing in the SDK or use a pinned adapter tested
with method errors, invalid requests, malformed frames and notifications.
The compliant handshake, IDs and clean EOF passed independently.

M3 | Input types and schema | Partially fixed |
server/server.py:74-132, :190-217, plugin/Core/J.cs:29-62
The public tool schema exposes action as a string and params as an open
dictionary. It cannot tell clients which fields or types a nested operation
requires. Native string/choice helpers also treat invalid non-string values
as absent in some paths. The patch validates the affected dry_run and QA
inputs, removes the duplicate WaterGEMS import target description and
validates the help topic. Define typed per-action and per-operation schemas
and generate descriptions from them. Preserve a compatibility path for the
existing action/params API. Use strict validation for values that select or
change drawing objects.

M4 | Inconsistent multi-read QA | Fixed | server/qa.py:41-63
The check ran four requests using whichever drawing was active at each call.
A drawing or Civil 3D instance change could mix unrelated results. The first
reply binds the target when omitted, or the caller can pass a known target.
All remaining reads use that identity. The result includes the target.

M5 | Sheet retry work | Fixed | server/sheets.py:355-387
Retry discovery had no per-stage scan bound and accepted any state=error
for resubmission. The patch limits lookup to eight attempt IDs per stage,
resumes only known pre-start errors and refuses unknown outcomes for
inspection. Applied-stage receipts and known rollback handling are retained.

M6 | Unbounded regex and file parsing | Open, input-dependent |
server/qa.py:14-29, server/sewergems.py:69-91, server/watergems.py:78-123
Layer QA matches an unrestricted caller-provided Python regex synchronously
over up to 20,000 layers. Workbook/CSV readers materialize records without a
cell/row or expanded-byte budget before later model limits. The worker model
cannot safely interrupt that CPU work. Use a safe regex subset or an isolated
worker with a deadline and limit workbook entries, expanded bytes and rows.

M7 | Transport bounds and teardown | Partially fixed |
server/bridge_client.py:83-153, plugin/Bridge/BridgeServer.cs:144-244
The previous private transport accepted partial EOF frames and allowed long
idle connections. The patch requires complete frames, caps discovery and
response frames, validates basic envelope fields and shortens idle slots.
Socket reads still use a per-operation timeout, public SDK stdio has no
application frame cap, and private connections share a 16-slot pool before
authentication. Bridge shutdown cancels the listener without tracking or
awaiting active handlers. Use per-call monotonic deadlines, bounded frame
parsing, a short separate pre-authentication budget, reserved status capacity
and a tracked shutdown for listeners and clients.

M8 | Multi-instance ownership | Open, conditional on concurrent startup or PID reuse |
plugin/Bridge/BridgeServer.cs:40-108, :133-159
Descriptor replacement is atomic per write, but owner lookup, publication,
shutdown deletion and handoff are separate operations. The liveness test
identifies the owner by PID alone. Competing start/stop events can race, and a
stale descriptor can appear live if Windows has reused the PID. Serialize
election/publication with a named lock. Validate owner identity with the
session ID and process start time under that lock.

M9 | Read-only classification and hints | Partially fixed |
server/server.py:187-188, plugin/Read/ViewRead.cs:72-97
The read tool can change the active view, layout and implied selection via
show_objects. Both tool groups previously advertised a closed world despite
user-selected local file access. The patch makes the open-world hint accurate.
Expose interactive view/selection operations in a distinct tool if the
read-only client contract is intended to exclude UI changes.

M10 | Long-running requests and retries | Open, input-dependent |
plugin/Bridge/MainThread.cs:31-71, plugin/Bridge/BridgeServer.cs:288-301
The queue timeout abandons the work atomically but the posted callback still
has to drain from Civil 3D's UI context. Repeated busy pings can accumulate
abandoned callbacks while the UI is blocked. Status stays independent of UI
dispatch. Coalesce ping probes and use a bounded, drainable work queue.

Low
---
L1 | Dependency and release reproducibility | Partially fixed |
server/requirements.txt:1-5 and build_package.bat:28-29
Application code directly uses AnyIO, Pydantic and typing-extensions. Those
requirements are now declared, but the resolver still accepts a broad MCP
version range and the live audit covers one version. Pin the SDK for shipped
packages and run the conformance suite before expanding the tested range.

L2 | Host metadata in errors | Open, source-confirmed |
server/bridge_client.py:109-138 and plugin/Core/WriteGate.cs:19-29
Some user-visible messages include a full local descriptor or audit-log path.
Native error text also forwards the underlying exception message. Return safe
client-facing fields and keep detailed host diagnostics in local logs.
No credential value or full exception stack was observed in the tested tool
results.

L3 | Performance scaling and dead parameters | Open |
server/watergems.py:507-568, :612-627, :656-661 and :776-778
mains rebuilds and sorts a forest for each extracted path. The repeated
component scan can be quadratic on fragmented networks. _summary rescans all
pipes for each material-and-size group. The phase argument to _edit and
stage argument to failed are unused. Use a component-aware worklist and
one-pass aggregation, and remove dead arguments after checking callers.

Redundancies and behavior-preserving cleanup
-------------------------------------------
- Keep the legacy public tool while introducing a shared machine-readable
  action registry. The single tool currently advertises about 41,600
  description characters. Its shallow schema leaves routing and validation
  details in prose. Centralize metadata, validation and registration for
  Python and C#. Static checks now catch duplicate native registrations.
- A common stage coordinator can replace repeated receipt and recovery logic
  across WaterGEMS, SewerGEMS and sheets. First capture each workflow's dry-run,
  status, partial-commit and retry rules in fixtures. Keep the separate
  workflow semantics while factoring transport and receipt handling.
- Share workbook field parsing only where units, nullable values and accepted
  header aliases agree. Keep Civil 3D geometry calculations outside transport
  handlers. The source scan found no cross-client notification feedback loop
  or unbounded recursive traversal in the network-line walkers inspected.

Verification
------------
- The patched Python smoke suite passed. This includes raw MCP 2025-06-18
  negotiation, integer/string response IDs, notification silence, clean
  stdout framing and EOF, cancellation, tool errors, split and read-only
  modes, SewerGEMS, WaterGEMS and sheet fixtures, and generated-catalogue checks.
- The source MCP server negotiated 2025-11-25 against a live Civil 3D 2027
  bridge on unsaved Drawing1.dwg. Drawing and Civil object reads, targeted QA
  reads and stale drawing target rejection passed for both read and edit entry
  points. The scratch drawing still reported editing disabled. The native
  valid-target dry run, commit and rollback were blocked by that drawing's
  edit gate. The test drawing remains unsaved.
- A live private bridge probe ignored an incomplete EOF frame and accepted the
  equivalent complete read request.
- Isolated raw stdio probes produced both SDK behaviors documented in M1
  and M2. Tested with MCP 1.30.0, AnyIO 4.15.1 and Pydantic 2.14.1.
- The real C# ledger source passed a harness for 8,192 entries, oldest-ID
  replay, a known pre-start timeout and an uncertain execution failure.
- Release build succeeded for Civil 3D 2024, 2025 and 2027. The build reported
  34 existing obsolete-API and nullable-assignment warnings and zero errors.
  Native 2024/2025, production DWGs, full imports, ChatGPT, Claude and the
  packaged distribution were outside the live run.

