File-by-file change log
-----------------------
server/server.py
  Added cancellation propagation, MCP error receipts and strict type checks
  for help topic, QA options and dry_run.
  Removed truthiness-based substitution of invalid empty params values.
  Modified default-name QA dispatch and open-world annotations.
  Why | Keep edit failures, client cancellation and public hints accurate.

server/bridge_client.py
  Added a per-call cancellation signal, discovery/request/reply size limits
  and descriptor/envelope validation.
  Removed acceptance of EOF without a newline as a complete reply.
  Modified connection/send handling to check cancellation before a send.
  Why | Avoid sending follow-up work and reject invalid bridge frames.

plugin/Bridge/MainThread.cs
  Added CadQueueTimeoutException after the atomic queued-to-abandoned
  transition.
  Modified queue timeout classification while retaining the existing wait for
  a delegate that has already started.
  Why | Give the edit ledger positive proof when a retry is safe.

plugin/Bridge/EditRequests.cs
  Added the retryable status field and a fail-closed session capacity check.
  Removed eviction of edit identities and blanket retry of all error states.
  Modified error replay to preserve terminal identity and status.
  Why | Avoid re-execution after history pressure or an ambiguous failure.

plugin/Bridge/BridgeServer.cs
  Removed acceptance of partial request lines at EOF.
  Modified the private idle timeout from ten minutes to five seconds.
  Why | Retain only complete frames and reduce idle slot occupancy.

server/qa.py
  Added optional target input and the resolved target in the default-name
  report.
  Modified the lookups to keep each result tied to the same open drawing.
  Why | Prevent cross-drawing QA summaries during document switching.

server/sheets.py
  Added an eight-attempt lookup cap and terminal handling of uncertain errors.
  Removed unbounded attempt lookup and blanket error replay.
  Why | Bound retry discovery and respect the native ledger's safety rule.

server/sewergems.py
  Modified finish recovery to resend a known pre-start queue timeout under the
  original finish ID. Terminal failures keep their recorded receipt.
  Why | Allow safe recovery without recreating the committed core network.

server/catalog.py
  Removed the duplicate optional WaterGEMS import target entry.
  Modified edit retry guidance and documented optional target for default-name
  QA.
  Why | Advertise the same preconditions and retry behavior as the code.

server/requirements.txt
  Added explicit AnyIO, Pydantic and typing-extensions requirements.
  Why | Record directly imported dependencies for source and package installs.

docs/ACTIONS.md
  Regenerated the action reference from the catalogue.
  Why | Keep the published tool descriptions aligned with the implementation.

tests/smoke_test.py
  Added raw stdio handshake/frame checks, cancellation and declined-error
  checks, dry_run type checks, drawing identity assertions and duplicate
  registry checks. Added the SewerGEMS unit suite to the smoke entry point.
  Why | Cover the changed public behavior and catch silent registration drift.

tests/live_protocol_test.py
  Added a test for source stdio against a blank native drawing, with an
  explicit edit mode for dry run, rollback, commit, replay and cleanup.
  Why | Verify the same protocol path the client uses against the real add-in.

tests/sheets_test.py
  Added cases for an uncertain edit, a safe same-ID retry and a saturated
  per-stage retry chain.
  Why | Verify the sheet workflow respects the edit ledger and lookup bound.

tests/sewergems_test.py
  Added a pre-start queue timeout to the finish-stage recovery fixture and
  asserted that finishing reuses its ID before advancing a known rollback.
  Why | Distinguish safe same-ID recovery from a fresh transaction attempt.

tests/results/protocol_audit_20261125/LedgerAudit.csproj and Program.cs
  Added a local audit harness that compiles the real ledger source with small
  stubs for Autodesk-dependent types and drives its capacity and retry cases.
  Build outputs follow the workspace's ignored test-results convention.

tests/results/protocol_audit_20261125/installed_2027_backup/C3dMcpBridge.dll
  Added a backup of the previously installed Civil 3D 2027 binary. Deployed the
  built DLL for the live session and confirmed its SHA-256 matched the build.
  Why | Make the installed change reversible and verify the tested binary.

docs/MCP_PROTOCOL_AUDIT.log
  Added this audit, verification record and per-file change log.
